# CODEOWNERS — defines who must review changes before merge.
#
# Prefer GitHub teams (@org/team) as owners: ownership survives staff changes
# and a whole team shares the review load. Solo-maintained repos can list an
# individual (@username) directly and swap in a team once one exists — an
# accurate individual owner beats an aspirational team that doesn't exist yet.
# The ruleset on main has "require code owner review" enabled, so any PR that
# touches a path below requires approval from the listed owner.
#
# NOTE for solo repos: GitHub blocks self-approval. A sole codeowner behind
# "require code owner review" with no ruleset bypass actor can never merge —
# harden_repo.sh detects this and offers --allow-admin-bypass.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins for a given file.

# Default owner for everything in the repo.
*                       @melampus-admin

# Lock down the automation and governance surface specifically — changes here
# affect every deployment and the protection rules themselves.
/.github/               @melampus-admin
/.github/workflows/     @melampus-admin

# The published site (served folder). Point this at a content/docs team if that differs from
# the platform owners; otherwise leave it as the default owner.
/site/                  @melampus-admin
